      "modifications": [
        "Converted the original COLLADA geometry and compatible authored Idle, Walk and Trot clips to self-contained GLB with Three.js 0.170.0. Preserved original mesh topology and UVs; no invented primitive horse geometry and no artificial polygon inflation.",
        "Joined body, mane, tail, quilted leather riding pad and bridle/reins from the official matching 0 A.D. horse art. Rebound the four accessory meshes to the same 86 named bone nodes after verifying inverse bind matrices. Kept prop_rider and prop_saddle sockets.",
        "Embedded the original diffuse and normal PNG maps. Used rough nonmetallic PBR materials. Kept the mane/tail strand alpha mask; interpreted the riding pad texture alpha as its original player-colour data, not opacity, so the pad remains opaque. Omitted source specular maps rather than incorrectly treating them as metallic-roughness data.",
        "Removed source workstation image/material paths before conversion and assigned only explicitly downloaded embedded textures. The final GLB has no external image or buffer URIs.",
        "Added a small vertical HorseGrounding track sampled at 120 Hz to compensate for negative hoof heights in the source body/animation combination while preserving above-ground and airborne poses. Maximum pre-normalization corrections were Idle: 0.012243 source units, Walk: 0.163423 source units, Trot: 0.094738 source units.",
        "Translated and uniformly scaled the complete rig to face +Z in a Y-up, metre-based frame. Centered and fitted the sampled body, mane, tail, pad and bridle sweep inside a 1.535 m horizontal radius, leaving margin inside 1.55 m. Retained natural anatomy. Omitted Gallop, whose longer tail/hoof sweep would require a materially smaller horse for the same cavalry clearance.",
        "Optimized redundant animation keyframes without removing joints or authored motion. This GLB adaptation remains licensed CC-BY-SA-3.0."
      ],
